{ Against an early c4, do not use the full Taimanov setup. Fianchetto with ...g6 and ...Bg7, and consider ...Nge7. This differs from 5.c4 in the Maroczy chapter, where Black has already entered an Open Sicilian. Aman also plays the same structure with White so that the familiar squares are learned with colors reversed. } 1. c4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 g6 { Fianchetto rather than playing ...Be7. } 4. g3 Bg7 5. Bg2 e6 6. O-O Nge7 { The knight stays out of the bishop's diagonal and supports ...b5. } *

